  "summary": "The study compares three wet-spun Ti3C2Tx/aramid nanofiber (T/A) fiber electrodes: T/A-0, T/A-2, and T/A-5, containing 0%, 2%, and 5% ANF, respectively. Ti3C2Tx was produced by HF etching of Ti3AlC2, TMAOH-assisted delamination, and wet spinning in a 0.5 m FeCl2 coagulation bath. The headline T/A-5 fiber delivered 807 F cm\u22123 (278 F g\u22121) at 3 A cm\u22123 in 3 m H2SO4, while exhibiting 104 MPa tensile strength. The authors additionally assembled T/A-5 symmetric FSCs using PVA-H2SO4 and F-MMT/PVA-H2SO4/DMSO electrolytes, but these are device/electrolyte configurations using the same T/A-5 electrode rather than distinct electrode materials. Mass loading, fiber thickness, BET area, pore metrics, and tortuosity were not reported."
